/E (A flat liststores each stop as \(train number, train name, station, arrival, departure, running days\). Every query scans all stoprecords and checks station and day, costing O\(total stops\) time and O\(total stops\) storage. A station index built over theflatlist can reduce a query to O\(trains at the station\), but requires extra index space. The nested timetable withoutanindex also scans all trains/stops; the nested timetable with an index has faster repeated station queries. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
